Test network. This app talks to the project's pool on Base Sepolia (chain id 84532, a Base test network, not Ethereum Sepolia). Every token here is a test token with no value, and no real person has borrowed from this pool.

Pool 0x73872b8fb7f1771c67911f03edc75abdc9514973, deployed from contract commit 1812e7d; this page was built from commit 258affb. Your wallet signs and pays for each transaction: you need a little Base Sepolia ETH for gas and test USDC from Circle's faucet. A new wallet has no credit to borrow against until someone who holds credit backs it or an issuer grants it a line. Step-by-step walkthrough: test gas, test USDC, credit, the wallet prompts and what to do after a rejected or lost transaction.
